course: dictionary
lesson: 3271
title: Names of places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A name that starts with a capital letter is a proper noun. It names one particular place, person or thing. «Erie» is a proper noun: it names one special lake, not any lake.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the name. «The Erie Canal, opened in 1825, linked the Great Lakes to the Hudson River.» The word canal tells you Erie is a waterway, and linked tells you it joins places together.
explain: Some names are used for more than one thing. Erie is the name of a lake, a city and an old Native American people, so the words around it show which one is meant. In «Lake Erie», it is the lake; the city of Erie is in Pennsylvania, USA.
fact: Erie is one of the five Great Lakes of North America, between the USA and Canada.
fact: Its full name is Lake Erie.
fact: Erie is also a city in Pennsylvania, USA, on the shore of Lake Erie.
fact: Lake Erie is the shallowest of the Great Lakes, so it warms up quickly in summer and freezes over in winter.
fact: The Erie Canal is a famous old canal in New York State, opened in 1825.
exercise: What kind of word is Erie in «Lake Erie»? | *A proper noun, a name for one particular place | A verb, a doing word | An adjective, a describing word | A plural noun for many lakes
exercise: «The Erie Canal, opened in 1825, linked the Great Lakes to the Hudson River.» What did the Erie Canal link? | *The Great Lakes and the Hudson River | Only the Hudson River | The sea and a desert | Two cities in Canada
exercise: Lake Erie is one of the Great Lakes. Where is it? | Under the sea in Africa | In Australia | *Between the USA and Canada | In the middle of Scotland
test: Which of the five Great Lakes is the shallowest, so it warms up quickly in summer? | Lake Superior | Lake Michigan | Lake Ontario | *Lake Erie
test: The city of Erie is in which place? | New York State | *Pennsylvania, USA | Scotland | Ontario, Canada
exam: In «The Erie Canal opened in 1825», what does Erie name? | A lake in Africa | The name of a dog | *A famous old canal in New York State | A city in Canada
